   "question": "Under the Data Protection Act 2018, what is the minimum age at which a child can consent to information society services in the UK?",
   "answer": "The minimum age at which a child can consent to information society services in the UK under the Data Protection Act 2018 is 13 years old. ⚖️",
   "why": "The legislation (Section 9 of the Data Protection Act 2018) modifies Article 8(1) of the UK GDPR so that references to '16 years' are read as '13 years' for information society services. The ICO's current guidance confirms that only children aged 13 and over can give their own consent when an ISS is offered directly to them and consent is the lawful basis.",
